From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0/10] ASoC: qcom: make speaker protection safe to require

Speaker protection in codec DMA lane order, a V/I guard in the
amplifier and WSA macro, calibration results reported but never
applied, one checked SP RX/SP VI pass, and a DT property that makes
protection mandatory, with the sm8250 and wsa8840 bindings.

 1/10 ASoC: dt-bindings: qcom,sm8250: add WSA speaker protection properties
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 2/10 ASoC: dt-bindings: qcom,sm8250: allow 18 codec DAIs on a link
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 3/10 ASoC: qcom: run speaker protection in codec DMA lane order
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 4/10 ASoC: dt-bindings: qcom,wsa8840: add speaker protection properties
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 5/10 ASoC: codecs: wsa884x: add a V/I guard: no PA without V/I sense
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 6/10 ASoC: codecs: lpass-wsa-macro: refuse V/I capture without V/I inputs
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 7/10 ASoC: qcom: audioreach: report VI calibration results, never apply them
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 8/10 ASoC: qcom: audioreach: configure SP RX and SP VI in one checked pass
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
 9/10 ASoC: qcom: x1e80100: require speaker protection when the DT says so
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.
10/10 ASoC: qcom: q6apm: refuse graphs that tap another graph's SP VI subgraph
     Author: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
     Not posted.

From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:09:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/10] ASoC: dt-bindings: qcom,sm8250: add WSA speaker protection
 properties

Describe what the x1e80100 and glymur cards need to run DSP speaker
protection with V/I feedback from the WSA884x amplifiers:

- qcom,wsa-speaker-lanes: the codec DMA lane of each V/I speaker. On
  Glymur the lanes alternate between the WSA and WSA2 macros, so link
  order is not the lane order calibration and tuning data use.
- qcom,speaker-protection-required: the speakers must not play without
  speaker protection. They run at the amplifiers' operating point if
  every amplifier has one and qcom,vi-guard, else at conservative gain
  limits.
- qcom,uefi-speaker-calibration, qcom,speaker-r0-range-micro-ohms: the
  factory R0/T0 is in the UEFI variable SmartAmpCalibrationData, and
  its R0 values must lie in the given range.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml           | 61 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
index e2e3fc99e6d9..78363c30edbe 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,sm8250.yaml
@@ -76,6 +76,47 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
     description: User visible long sound card name
 
+  qcom,wsa-speaker-lanes:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 4
+    uniqueItems: true
+    items:
+      maximum: 3
+    description:
+      WSA codec DMA lane of each amplifier with a V/I sense DAI on the WSA
+      playback link, in sound-dai order. Each lane 0..n-1 appears once.
+      Speakers are numbered in lane order, the order of the per-speaker
+      calibration and tuning data.
+
+  qcom,speaker-protection-required:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The speakers on the WSA playback link must not be driven without DSP
+      speaker protection fed by V/I sense from every amplifier. If every
+      amplifier on the link has qcom,vi-guard and an operating point
+      (qcom,pa-gain-max-millidecibel and qcom,speaker-full-scale-microvolt),
+      the speakers may run at it; otherwise they are held at conservative
+      gain limits.
+
+  qcom,uefi-speaker-calibration:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The factory speaker calibration is in the UEFI variable
+      SmartAmpCalibrationData, vendor GUID
+      53559579-8753-4f5c-9130-e82acfb8d893, in the Qualcomm layout (72 bytes,
+      little endian - number of speakers, R0 per speaker in ohms as Q24, T0
+      per speaker in degrees Celsius as Q6, valid flag), speakers in lane
+      order.
+
+  qcom,speaker-r0-range-micro-ohms:
+    items:
+      - description: Lowest plausible factory R0 of the board's speakers
+      - description: Highest plausible factory R0 of the board's speakers
+    description:
+      Range every speaker's factory R0 read from UEFI must be in; a value
+      outside it means the variable is not usable on this board.
+
 patternProperties:
   ".*-dai-link$":
     description:
@@ -154,6 +195,26 @@ required:
   - compatible
   - model
 
+dependentRequired:
+  qcom,uefi-speaker-calibration: [ 'qcom,speaker-r0-range-micro-ohms' ]
+  qcom,speaker-protection-required: [ 'qcom,wsa-speaker-lanes' ]
+
+allOf:
+  - if:
+      not:
+        properties:
+          compatible:
+            contains:
+              enum:
+                - qcom,glymur-sndcard
+                - qcom,x1e80100-sndcard
+    then:
+      properties:
+        qcom,wsa-speaker-lanes: false
+        qcom,speaker-protection-required: false
+        qcom,uefi-speaker-calibration: false
+        qcom,speaker-r0-range-micro-ohms: false
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
