From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:10:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/10] ASoC: qcom: run speaker protection in codec DMA lane order

The SP/VI code assumed speaker n is codec DMA lane n and that link
codec order is speaker order. On Glymur the WSA lanes alternate between
the WSA and WSA2 macros, so four amplifiers in link order sit on lanes
0, 2, 1, 3, while the factory R0/T0 and SP/VI tuning are in lane order:
speakers 1 and 2 got each other's calibration and tuning.

Register the VI speakers in lane order from "qcom,wsa-speaker-lanes",
failing the card unless it is a permutation matching the speaker count.
audioreach builds the VI channel map from that, with each 32-bit V/I
word mapped as I then V as it lies in memory, resends it after the
static cfg blob, and refuses SP RX/VI unless the speakers were
registered in lane order for the graph's channel count.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
