Subject: [PATCH 5/10] ASoC: codecs: wsa884x: add a V/I guard: no PA without V/I
 sense

Speaker protection estimates coil temperature and excursion from the
amplifier's V/I sense; without that stream the DSP protects on stale or
no data. With "qcom,vi-guard", unmute keeps the PA off unless the
amplifier is attached and its VISENSE port is enabled and prepared;
mute and VISENSE PRE_DEPREP switch the PA off, checked by readback and
retried until it reads off, and a detach leaves it off in the cache
for the reattach; the VISENSE Switch cannot
change while the port is prepared, and V/I capture with it off is
refused.

The off write takes its runtime PM reference before the guard's lock,
as resuming the bus reports status, which takes that lock. Under the
SoundWire bus lock it does not resume and leaves a suspended amplifier
to the retry.

