A V/I capture with no 'WSA_AIF_VI Mixer' input enabled gives speaker
protection no feedback, but hw_params accepts it. Refuse it, and lock
the mixer from AIF_VI hw_params to hw_free so V/I feedback cannot be
switched off under a running speaker protection graph.

The mixer state and the AIF_VI reservation share one lock. The mixer
put's DAPM update takes the card locks, so it runs after that lock is
dropped, and hw_params refuses V/I capture while a put is in progress.

