From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:12:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/10] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: report VI calibration results, never
 apply them

A successful VI calibration run replaced the cached R0/T0 used by the
next Normal mode graph. The result depends on conditions the kernel
cannot check (a quiet, cold speaker at a known temperature and level),
and a wrong R0 makes the thermal model misjudge the coil temperature.

Only log the result, one line per speaker; R0/T0 stays what the
"Speaker Protection R0T0" control or the factory calibration set. An
event for a different speaker count than armed, or claiming more
speakers than it carries, fails the run. Clear the per-speaker states
and R0 of "Speaker Protection Calibration State" when a run is armed,
and log a run number, so it never shows an earlier run's result.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
