From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:06:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/10] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: configure SP RX and SP VI in one
 checked pass

SP RX and SP VI are configured from the global operation mode, which
can change between the two modules' media format calls, and nothing
checks that a WSA RX graph configured both.

Make a WSA RX backend prepare one speaker protection setup pass, owned
by its graph and taking the mode once: a pass that configures only one
of the two modules fails the prepare, and either module configured
outside a pass is refused. With audioreach_sp_set_required(), a WSA RX
graph without both modules fails its prepare.

